ock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106220","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106220","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106220.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106220.patch","merged_at":"2025-06-08T22:51:24Z"},"body":"Fixes #70973. This PR fixes the ability to import and export glTF files with buffers larger than 4 GiB.\r\n\r\nI tested this with the https://github.com/Rytelier/Godot-4-forest-benchmark project linked in issue #70973. In master, Godot crashes. With this PR, Godot successfully exports the file, though it does take a minute, and the resulting `.bin` file is 4,308,900,759 bytes.\r\n\r\nI tested importing this file back in. It loads correctly in Blender, but it takes about an hour, and then Blender uses 30 GiB of RAM. I tried loading it into Godot, and the glTF code succeeds at importing the file, but Godot stalls when trying to save the imported scene, specifically `ResourceFormatSaverBinaryInstance::save` gets stuck in calling `_find_resources` over and over, until it uses about 30 GiB of RAM and the CPU usage stalls at 0%, but it seems to still be calling that function. Anyway, I don't know how to fix that, but it's not a bug with the glTF code.\r\n\r\nNote that the integer sizes in GLTFAccessor and GLTFBufferView were increased, affecting the exposed API.","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"ht